After your ROUND-OK on Findings 1-21, the user picked routes for three deferred items and the fixer implemented them. Evaluate each against its stated requirement (quoted below), and report defects the change introduced. The Kotlin cannot be compiled here — review it by reading (check Android API usage, threading, lifetimes of file descriptors and URI grants).

## R1 (pass1-D3) — Android local player must read via the system grant, not paths
A real-device probe (OnePlus, Android 16, app holds NO storage permissions; folder /sdcard/Download/LPTest owned by another app with lptest.mp4 + lptest.danmaku.xml + lptest.zh-CN.srt) showed:
- "打开视频文件" (LocalPlayer.pickFile → FilePicker.pickFiles): the video plays, but the whole 47.84 MB file was copied into cache/file_picker (app cache 0 → 48.87 MB), and the side danmaku/subtitle files were NOT found (it looks next to the cache copy).
- "打开视频文件夹" (LocalPlayer.pickFolder → FilePicker.getDirectoryPath → path + Directory.listSync): the user granted the folder in the system dialog, yet the app showed "没有找到可播放的视频文件" — a path listing cannot see files through a SAF tree grant without storage permission.
User's pick: read through the system grant (Storage Access Framework), no copying, no new storage permission.
Requirements:
- Folder: use the granted tree URI (persist it with takePersistableUriPermission) and list its children through DocumentsContract via a platform channel in android/app/src/main/kotlin/.../MainActivity.kt (a `librepili/media` channel already exists there). Find the video and its side files (librepili.json, <base>.danmaku.xml / <base>.xml, <base>.*.srt, <base>.comments.json, comments_images/, cover) exactly as the desktop path does.
- Video playback from the content:// URI without copying. First verify in the pub cache how media_kit/libmpv on Android handles content:// URIs (or an fd:// from openFileDescriptor) and use what actually works; report what you verified.
- Small side files (xml/srt/json/images): read their bytes through the content resolver (copying only these small files into a per-video app cache folder is acceptable if that is how the existing loaders consume them; clean that cache when the player closes or on next open). The multi-GB video must never be copied.
- File mode ("打开视频文件"): open the chosen file by URI without copying (check whether the android_file_picker SAF options avoid the copy — read FileUtils.openFileStream/addFile; if not, use ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT through the channel). In single-file mode Android gives no access to neighbours, so after opening, if no side files are reachable, show a one-line hint that on Android "打开视频文件夹" loads danmaku/subtitles/comments.
- Progress key / playlist for URI sources must be stable (e.g. hash of the document URI).
- Desktop/iOS behaviour unchanged. Folders the app itself created under Download/LibrePili/<title>/ must keep working (path access still fine there; either path works).
- Unit-test what is testable in Dart (side-file matching on a list of names); the channel itself is verified later on the device by the orchestrator.

## R2 (pass2-D2) — make multi-segment merges not fail
Finding (pass 2): when Type1 (durl) segments cannot be joined/remuxed, they are kept as separate parts and in-app playback plays only part 1. The user rejected both "play all parts" and "just warn": they want the merge itself to succeed. Eliminate the fallback causes as far as possible:
- MP4 segments whose `stsd` (codec config) differ: MP4 allows several sample entries per track — join by emitting all distinct sample entries in stsd and pointing each chunk's stsc sample_description_index at the right one, instead of throwing UnsupportedError.
- FLV: codec config (AVC sequence header / AudioSpecificConfig) that changes mid-stream or between segments → same multi-sample-entry approach. Also support HEVC in FLV if Bilibili can deliver it (check both the legacy codec id 12 convention and Enhanced-RTMP FourCC 'hvc1'); if you conclude it cannot occur for bilibili durl, say why.
- Corrupt/truncated segment (FormatException while reading): treat as a download problem — re-download that segment (bounded retries) and retry the merge — instead of falling back.
- Keep the separate-parts fallback only for genuinely impossible cases (e.g. a codec with no MP4 mapping), and list exactly which cases remain.
Add unit tests on synthetic data for each newly-handled case (different stsd across segments; config change mid-FLV).

## R3 (pass2-D3) — desktop export folder colliding with internal folders
Finding (pass 2): on desktop `_exportDir()` returns the download root itself; export folders are named after the sanitised title while internal page folders are `<avid>` / `s_<seasonId>`. A title like "114514" exports into `<root>/114514/`, a later download of av114514 creates `<root>/114514/c_<cid>` inside it, and deleting that later download recursively deletes the kept export.
User's pick: detect the collision and rename. Export names that could collide with the internal layout (all-digit names, `s_<digits>`, and any existing internal page folder) get a distinguishing change so export folders and internal folders can never be the same directory — in both directions (a new internal folder must not land inside an existing export folder either; check how internal folders are named and whether that side needs a guard). Add a unit test for the naming rule.



