  989:   /// Names of the internal page folders in the download root: `<avid>` and
  990:   /// `s_<seasonId>` (case-insensitive: Windows folder names are).
  991:   static final _internalPageName = RegExp(r'^(s_)?\d+$', caseSensitive: false);
  992: 
  993:   /// On desktop exports share the download root with the internal page
  994:   /// folders, so an export named like one (a title such as "114514") would
  995:   /// be the same directory as that video's download. Such names get a
  996:   /// suffix; no internal folder is ever named like the result.
  997:   @visibleForTesting
  998:   static String exportFolderName(String name) =>
  999:       _internalPageName.hasMatch(name) ? '$name (视频)' : name;
 1000: 
 1001:   /// Internal page folders hold only entry folders; a folder with files at
 1002:   /// its top level is an export (or the user's own) that happens to carry
 1003:   /// the page folder's name.
 1004:   static bool _isForeignFolder(Directory dir) =>
 1005:       dir.listSync().any((e) => e is File);
