codex
- [REGRESSED] R1 — SAF route is conceptually implemented, but the new Dart file does not compile.
  The Android picker/channel path avoids `file_picker` video copies and uses `content://` plus `fdclose://`, with side files mirrored into cache. However `LocalDocuments.match` calls `firstOrNull` without importing the collection extension, so this change breaks the build at `lib/services/local_documents.dart:139` and `:162`.

- [RESOLVED] R2 — merge path now handles the requested codec-config cases and treats damaged segments as download failures.
  MP4 joins now preserve distinct sample entries and sample-description indexes, FLV config changes become multiple entries, and HEVC FLV variants are covered. Damaged/missing Type1 segments are prechecked and re-downloaded with bounded retries before merge; remaining fallback is limited to unsupported mappings such as mixed FLV/MP4, track/codec changes, or unmapped codecs.

- [RESOLVED] R3 — export/internal folder collisions are guarded in both directions.
  Export folder names shaped like internal page roots get a non-internal suffix, and new downloads move aside old foreign/export folders before creating internal page directories. Deletion paths also avoid recursively deleting legacy export folders that already collide with an internal page name.

- [P1] Missing `firstOrNull` extension import breaks the build — lib/services/local_documents.dart:137-162
  `videos.firstOrNull` and `.where(...).firstOrNull` require the collection extension, but `local_documents.dart` imports only Flutter services/foundation and `path`. Add `package:collection/collection.dart` with the needed extension, or replace these with explicit empty checks.

